  "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
  "relevance_note": "This adult allo-HSCT cohort of 10 includes one patient with 'haploinsufficiency of A20 (HA20) (n = 1)' (Patient #9, 'IEI HA20'), but the text never prints the gene symbol TNFAIP3 or the variant ('details on mutations in Online Resource Table S1'), so the flag rests on the authors' HA20 diagnosis and no variants row could be filled.",
  "method_note": "Read the paper in full and transcribed by hand (no table-parsing script); a Python script only assembled the JSON and checked spans and fields. Tables 1 and 2 have patients as rows (column '#'); Patient #9 is the only person with HA20 ('IEI HA20'). The other nine patients have other diagnoses (CTLA4HI, APDS, DOCK8, ALPS, DADA2, VEXAS, CVID2) and were deliberately not extracted, since none is described as carrying a TNFAIP3/A20 variant. No variants row: TNFAIP3 and the variant appear only in supplementary Table S1, which is not in the text. Table 1 'Age' (23) was read as age at allo-HSCT (the ten ages give the stated mean of 32.1, range 21-51), so it went into treatment_summary, not last evaluation; follow-up was 17 months (Table 2). vital_status 'alive' is inferred: the only death is patient #6 (Table 2 dagger; 'patient #6 died of COVID 19 infection'), and 'the nine patients who were alive' account for the rest. Excluded features with evidence_basis 'inferred from group statement' come from cohort-wide negatives ('No cases of limited or extensive chronic GvHD were reported.'; 'No patient experienced EBV reactivation after αβTCR/CD19 depletion') or a statement naming its only exception (no severe infections leading to hospitalization beyond the first 3 months except patient #6). Checklist: only 'gastrointestinal ulcers or inflammation' is observed (refractory colitis); everything else is not reported. Not recorded as phenotypes: CMV/EBV serostatus, IDDA (92 to 24 at 1 year), Karnofsky 40, HCT-CI 1. Contradictions in the paper (none bear on Patient #9's checklist): the abstract says '5 patients developed grade 2–4 acute GvHD', the results 'Four patients developed aGvHD of grade 2–4'; mixed chimerism is given for 'Patients #5 and #8' in the results and 'Patients #5 and #6' in the discussion; the eligibility window is 2019–2023 in one sentence and 2019–2024 in another; and 'median decrease in IDDA score was 3 (range 15–68)' does not fit inside its own range.",
